ion points for market entities and accounting for transformer/line losses if necessary.\"<|>\"infrastructure, measurement\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"结算依据\"<|>\"The electricity trading institution issues the settlement basis to market entities after collecting metering data, handles disputes, and organizes consultations for unavailable data.\"<|>\"financial settlement, data management\"<|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"送端地区\"<|>\"受端地区\"<|>\"Generators from the sending-end area involved in cross-regional transactions are managed under the auxiliary service scope of the receiving-end area and receive/pay compensation accordingly.\"<|>\"cross-regional management, auxiliary services\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"辅助服务\"<|>\"需求侧\"<|>\"Auxiliary services encourage participation from the demand-side (power users), who must meet technical requirements and receive compensation under unified standards.\"<|>\"market participation, grid stability\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"偏差考核费用\"<|>\"Power users bear responsibility for over/under consumption deviations and pay corresponding deviation penalty fees, which are then proportionally returned to generators.\"<|>\"deviation responsibility, financial penalty\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"优先发电\"<|>\"基数电量\"<|>\"Priority generation and base electricity together constitute a generator's base contract volume, both settled at government-approved prices before market contract volumes.\"<|>\"base contract components, regulated pricing\"<|>10)##\n(\"content_keywords\"<|>\"electricity market, contract deviation, auxiliary services, settlement mechanism, grid operation\")<|COMPLETE|>"
