ng Institutions manage the entire market registration process for new entrants.\"<|>\"registration management, market entry\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"市场注销\"<|>\"Electricity Trading Institutions handle deregistration applications and finalize exit procedures after obligations are met.\"<|>\"deregistration process, market exit\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电网企业\"<|>\"保底供电\"<|>\"Grid Companies are obligated to provide backup power supply at premium prices to users who exit the market without justification.\"<|>\"emergency supply, regulatory obligation\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"各省（区、市）价格主管部门\"<|>\"保底供电\"<|>\"Provincial price authorities determine the specific premium price levels for backup power supply within national frameworks.\"<|>\"price regulation, cost determination\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家能源局\"<|>\"市场注册\"<|>\"Market registration information managed by Electricity Trading Institutions is filed with the National Energy Administration and its branches.\"<|>\"regulatory oversight, compliance filing\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"零售交易\"<|>\"Electricity Users participate in the Retail Trading category, facing specific backup pricing rules if they deregister after trading.\"<|>\"consumer participation, pricing mechanism\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"售电公司\"<|>\"零售交易\"<|>\"Electricity Retail Companies operate within the Retail Trading category, providing services to end-users under market rules.\"<|>\"service provision, market role\"<|>8)##\n(\"content_keywords\"<|>\"electricity market regulation, market entry and exit, transaction settlement, backup power supply, pricing mechanisms\")<|COMPLETE|>"
